<title>UK: Smith &amp; Nephew buys S. Korean distributors.</title>
<headline>Smith &amp; Nephew buys S. Korean distributors.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Healthcare group Smith &amp; Nephew Plc said it had bought its South Korean distributors Yunhab Meditech and ChangMyung for around four million stg.</p>
<p>Smith &amp; Nephew said in a statement that combined sales of group products for the two companies totalled 4.5 million stg in 1995.</p>
<p>The new organisation will be renamed Smith &amp; Nephew Limited.</p>
<p>&quot;We now have a group presence in every major Asian market and will be able to focus our effort on becoming the leading supplier of tissue repair products in Asia,&quot; said chief executive John Robinson.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
